  "id": "binaural-beat",
  "term": "binaural beat",
  "definition": "A binaural beat is a perceived sound that can arise when different tones are presented to each ear. It is typically experienced as a fluctuation in loudness at smaller frequency differences, can sound like a rotating tone when the difference is very small, and tends to become a rough sound at larger differences.",
